# Where the app looks for the worker. Leave this UNSET for web development: the web build then
# follows whatever host served the page, so http://localhost:8082 uses the worker on localhost and
# http://192.168.1.20:8082 uses the worker on 192.168.1.20 — the same one, from both machines.
#
# Setting it pins every device to one address. That is what you want for a deployed worker, and for
# testing from a phone over Wi-Fi — but never pin it to `localhost`, which means "this machine": each
# device would end up on its own worker, in its own matchmaking queue, searching forever.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://vyra.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://<this-machine-lan-ip>:8787
#
# A pin wins over any address saved on the device from an earlier run, and the app rewrites that
# saved address on launch so a stale one cannot come back. Values here are inlined at BUILD time:
# restart Metro with --clear after editing, and add the matching web origin to CORS_ORIGINS in
# apps/worker/wrangler.local.jsonc.

# Temporary development bypass for the camera/pose step in the Arena flow (see
# src/lib/testMode.ts). Leave unset/false for the real camera. Never enable in a shipped build.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ARENA_TEST_MODE=true
